I walk on to the fish stall.
There are many fresh fish on the ice.
I point to a beautiful piece of salmon.
The fishmonger takes the salmon.
He weighs it on the scale.
"How much is that?" I ask.
"That will be seventy-two kroner," he answers.
He smiles at me.
He takes a yellow lemon from a box.
"A little free lemon for the fish," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say happily.
He wraps the fish and the lemon in paper.
I pay and put the package in my bag.
